  "sourceId": "thinksr",
  "title": "ThinkSR: compact thought, dense output",
  "lang": "en",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The method runs a dense carrier through four stages, while recurrence returns only to the DQ-CTM thought stage.",
      "claim": "ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.",
      "narration": "The image first becomes a dense feature field, because super-resolution needs spatial detail at every location. Windowing keeps that field local without discarding tokens. The compact thought process repeats inside the DQ-CTM block, with shared parameters across ticks. Decoding happens after the repeated thought updates, so the loop does not wrap the whole pipeline.",
